{"content":[{"c":["ARVAD, ARVADITE"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Small fortified island about 2 miles (3.2 kilometers) off the coast of Syria (ancient Phoenicia) and 30 miles (48 kilometers) north of Tripolis. Arvad developed a large trading and fighting fleet, and the fame of its sailors was referred to in a description of the naval power of Tyre (",{"href":"?bref=Ezek.27.8,11","r":"Ezek.27.8,11","rawR":"Ezek.27.8,11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezek.27.8,11","value":"Ezek.27.8,11"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ez 27:8, 11"},"). Egyptian records recount Arvad’s fall to Thutmose III about 1472 ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"},". Assyrian records indicate the importance of Arvad and its recurrent conquest by foreign powers from the 11th to the 7th centuries ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"},"."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":["Arvad was later known as Aradus or Arados, and is referred to as such in ",{"href":"?bref=1Macc.15.23","r":"1Macc.15.23","rawR":"1Macc.15.23","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Macc.15.23","value":"1Macc.15.23"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Maccabees 15:23"},". During the Persian and Hellenistic periods it was once again an important Mediterranean seaport, only to decline again. The Canaanite tribe of Arvadites (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.10.18","r":"Gen.10.18","rawR":"Gen.10.18","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.10.18","value":"Gen.10.18"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 10:18"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.1.16","r":"1Chr.1.16","rawR":"1Chr.1.16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.1.16","value":"1Chr.1.16"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 1:16"},") possibly had an ethnic connection with the island Arvad. Today Arvad is known as Ruad."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"ArvadArvadite","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Ez 27:8, 11","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ezek.27.8,11","rawQueryValue":"Ezek.27.8,11","sourceRefExact":"Ezek.27.8,11"},{"anchorText":"1 Maccabees 15:23","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Macc.15.23","rawQueryValue":"1Macc.15.23","sourceRefExact":"1Macc.15.23"},{"anchorText":"Gn 10:18","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.10.18","rawQueryValue":"Gen.10.18","sourceRefExact":"Gen.10.18"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 1:16","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.1.16","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.1.16","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.1.16"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"34bb1640a08e4d5e03e9f201b420cc75b48ba0f68ea6ac070cc643204034e9eb","sourceItemName":"ArvadArvadite","sourceItemOrder":514,"sourceMember":"Articles/A.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"ArvadArvadite","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Arvad, Arvadite","title":"Arvad, Arvadite","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}